  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, who serves as Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives of the Republic of Indonesia, has received endorsements for the vice presidential role from various stakeholders. Support has emerged from leaders of the National Mandate Party (PAN) and regional figures such as the Wali Nanggroe of Aceh, who described him as a young, visionary statesman. Political analysts point to his decades-long loyalty to President Prabowo Subianto and his role as a political bridge-builder across various factions as primary justifications for his candidacy. Former Minister of Tourism and Creative Economy Sandiaga Uno noted that the decision ultimately rests with President Prabowo Subianto. These discussions occur as the country observes broader political adjustments, including speculation regarding cabinet appointments and potential shifts in leadership roles. The developments reflect current efforts to ensure political stability within the administration and the legislative branch.",
